Review complete. All 8 angles run inline; the branch's own tests pass (`brainnotify`, `execx`, and the two new strategy tests ran green in a temp worktree, since removed). Plugin-side contract verified against the entire-brain repo: `memory notify --event checkpoint --session --branch` exists and the worker guard value is exactly `"1"`.

The dominant finding: the feature is dead for the default install mode. `cmd/entire/main.go` calls `restorePATH()` before `rootCmd.ExecuteContextC`, so every built-in command — including `entire hooks git post-commit` — runs with the user's original PATH. `NotifyCheckpoint` gates on `exec.LookPath("entire-brain")`, which only resolves PATH-installed plugins; managed installs (the standard flow, binaries in `PluginBinDir()`, deliberately not on PATH) never pass the gate, and the code comment asserts the opposite. Every test stubs `lookPath`, so the suite cannot see this.

